---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import headshot from "../assets/hs.jpg";
---

<Layout>
  <div id="main-content">
    <section id="header" class="text-center">
      <h1>About Me</h1>
    </section>
    <section id="about" class="text-center">
      <div class="about-container">
        <div class="about-image">
          <Image src={headshot} alt="brandon hernandez" />
        </div>
        <div class="about-content">
          <p>
            I came to imaging science from two directions at once. As a Computer
            Engineer, I needed to understand light. As a professional
            photographer, I needed to understand signals. Those two paths
            converged into a genuine fascination with the space where optics,
            hardware, and software have to agree on what reality looks like.<br> For
            four years, I've run a professional photography and video production
            business, owning every stage of the color pipeline — from RAW
            capture through final delivery in Lightroom and DaVinci Resolve —
            while managing client relationships from initial consultation
            through delivery. That work taught me that image quality isn't just
            a technical metric; it's a conversation between the sensor, the
            processing, and the person on the other end who needs to trust the
            result.<br> At NASA, I brought that same instinct into a research
            setting, analyzing Optical Coherence Tomography images to study how
            spaceflight affects astronaut vision — precise, high-stakes work
            where accuracy had real consequences. That combination of a
            photographer's eye, an engineer's discipline, and a scientist's
            approach to measurement is what I bring to technical work today. I'm
            currently building a from-scratch ISP pipeline in Python and NumPy,
            because I believe the best way to understand a system is to build it
            yourself — and the best way to deliver value from that system is to
            be able to explain it clearly to the people who depend on it.
          </p>
          <h2>Skills</h2>
          <div class="skills-badges">
            <span
              >Image Evaluation Metrics (MTF/SFR, SNR, DR, Color Accuracy)</span
            >
            <span>Camera Sensor Performance & Characterization</span>
            <span>ISP Pipeline Architecture (Demosaic, NR, Sharpening)</span>
            <span>Color Science & Tonal Reproduction</span>
            <span>Python (NumPy, OpenCV, Automation)</span>
            <span>C# / .NET</span>
            <span>SQL Server & Data Management</span>
            <span>Docker & CI/CD (GitHub Actions)</span>
            <span>Git</span>
            <span>Agile Methodology</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Experience</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>NASA Johnson Space Center:</strong> Analyzed Optical Coherence
              Tomography images to study structural changes in astronaut eyes resulting
              from extended spaceflight. Applied Python for data processing and database
              optimization in a high-precision research environment.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Harris County:</strong> Architected and built CAMS, a mission-critical
              full-stack web application for criminal justice case audit management,
              using .NET 8, C#, and SQL Server.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Brandon Hernandez Photography:</strong> Managed end-to-end
              imaging workflows across professional photography and 4K video production.
              Full color pipeline ownership including RAW processing, color calibration,
              LUT design, and color space management in Lightroom and DaVinci Resolve.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h2>Education</h2>
          <p>
            I hold both a Master of Science and a Bachelor of Science in
            Computer Engineering from the University of Houston-Clear Lake. My
            academic career focused on the intersection of hardware and
            software, providing me with the rigorous mathematical and
            signal-processing foundation required for advanced Image Quality
            Engineering and ISP evaluation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
